From 33aa0c3d06e98151200ee34fd5244187257932ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:33:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] feat(Detective #122): the ordered family's clamp is
 pinned by intent tests

The defect, verbatim. "`clamp` is not generated. The catalog marks it `unsupported`: clip(v, l, u) needs
the range the invariant names, and no premise for it is observed."

Why the obvious fix is wrong. Inventing a range makes the fence the engine's guess, and a clamp into the
observed [min, max] itself changes nothing (every observed value is inside it): it is a built-in
survivor. Def. 11.8(vii) names the narrowed range, so a value at an edge changes. The range IS observed:
the baseline records the minimum and maximum over the values a return site produced (38bec04), and the
clamp is generated into that range narrowed by one step on each side. A step is 1 for an int, the
adjacent float (math.nextafter), the adjacent Decimal, one day for a date, one microsecond for a naive
datetime or a timedelta; at a type's own limit it stays, so it cannot overflow. A range one step wide keeps
its upper edge (observed {0, 1} clamps into [1, 1]).

What each state means (`clamp_standing`, pinned): clamps / single_value (every observed value is the same:
nothing to narrow) / mixed_kinds (an int and a Decimal, or a date and a datetime, are not one ordered
range) / non_finite (a NaN or an infinity was returned) / not_ordered (a str, None, a list, an aware
datetime: not a clamp site, and no premise failed, so nothing is named). The three failed premises are
named per function in `mu_minus_withheld`. A bound travels in the mode as a token with no `:` (the
dimension separator): `return_clamp@i5,i9`, floats as `float.hex()`, dates as ordinals, datetimes and
timedeltas as microseconds, and round-trips for every kind including both extremes of each type.

What was NOT closed. Fraction is not an ordered kind the clamp supports (it has no adjacent value; the
site is not named, as it is typing not a failed premise), and neither is an aware datetime (its offset is
part of the value). Detective's harvest still carries type names (see 38bec04), so a Detective
`--two-sign` run does not yet generate the clamp.

Sensitivity: with the clamp tokens removed 10 of the 38 intent tests fail.
Pin: `clamp_standing` is pinned in 38bec04.

Tests: tests/test_mu_minus_clamp_premise_intent.py 38 passed; with the catalog, doc, policy and
instrumentation-ownership guards 109 passed under Python 3.14 and 109 under 3.12, PYTHONUNBUFFERED unset.
ruff clean under pinned 0.16.7.
